,"code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":", isn’t:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"list it beside the discovered ones, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DiscoveredEvent.all.map(\\.type) + [Legacy.self]"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Limits","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Limits"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An object file in a static archive that nothing references brings no record into the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"program: the linker leaves it out. That happens with CocoaPods’ static libraries, a static"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"XCFramework, or a Bazel library with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"alwayslink = False"},{"type":"text","text":". SwiftPM, and Bazel’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"alwayslink = True"},{"type":"text","text":", link every object file. Link such a library whole ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-force_load"},{"type":"text","text":" on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Apple platforms, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"--whole-archive"},{"type":"text","text":" on Linux) to have its events found."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent\/all"},{"text":" holds the events of the images loaded when it is called: the program and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dynamic libraries it links. A library opened later with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dlopen"},{"text":" adds its events from then on.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A module that declares events, linked into two images, lists each of its events twice, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stores and plans refuse the duplicate. Link each such m